# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `pylon dev` loads `.env` automatically.
#
# The app runs with no config: visitors can chat as guests and messages are
# saved. Replies need a model provider key. The key stays on the server.

# Model provider (required for replies)
#   PYLON_LLM_PROVIDER   "anthropic" | "openai"
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY    or OPENAI_API_KEY
# PYLON_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# OpenAI-compatible gateway (optional), such as OpenRouter:
#   PYLON_LLM_PROVIDER=openai
#   PYLON_LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api
#   OPENAI_API_KEY=<gateway key>
# Then list the gateway's model ids in lib/site.config.ts (chat.models).

# Site URL (optional)
# SITE_URL=https://yourchat.com
